# Cache + security headers.
#
# IN EFFECT. Cloudflare serves site/ as the Worker's static assets and applies
# this file — verified against the live site on 2026-09-29: main.js comes back
# "immutable" and every response carries X-Frame-Options. (An earlier note here
# said the opposite; that was true once and no longer is.) site/_redirects is
# applied the same way.
#
# vercel.json and netlify.toml mirror these rules in case the site ever moves.
#
# Because style.css and main.js are cached as immutable for a year, the build
# puts a content hash on every reference to them (style.css?v=<hash>). Without
# that, a returning visitor would keep the old file and never see a CSS change.
# A new stylesheet or script that is cached this way needs the same treatment:
# add it to VERSIONED in build/build.mjs.
#
# The rule that matters wherever it's applied: data.js and sanity-config.js must
# NEVER be cached as immutable. They are content, not code — caching them for a
# year means owner edits never reach anyone who has visited before.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/video/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/js/main.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/js/data.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/js/sanity-config.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
